s changed between two selected runs\" — the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data. So HLR-1 and HLR-3 are ONE capability: single epic covering both, at the higher priority P0. Do NOT split by priority.\n- HLR-2 (P1): Model Registry versions link back to runs, so comparison can be opened from registry. This spans Model Registry (backend linking) and Dashboard (opening comparison from registry). Actually HLR-2 says \"Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry.\" The linking is Model Registry work; opening a comparison from the registry involves Dashboard navigation. Hmm — could be one epic or two. Different component → separate epics per Rule 1. Model Registry: store/display run link on model version. Dashboard: deep-link into comparison view? Actually the Dashboard comparison view epic (HLR-1) builds the comparison surface; the registry link is a separate epic for Model Registry component.\n\nWait — where does Data Science Pipelines come in? Runs include pipeline runs; parameters/metrics for pipeline runs come from Data Science Pipelines. Possibly the run metadata backing. The strategy says \"training and pipeline runs\". Data Science Pipelines may need to expose run parameters/metrics for comparison — or it's passive (the Dashboard reads run data). Hmm. Let me check architecture context to understand.\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation covering comparison workflow from both runs list and registry → docs-authoring epic, blocked by all Implementation epics (Rule 11). Priority from strategy frontmatter priority: Major → P1.\n\nLet me look at .context/rhai-components.txt and architecture context directory.","signature":"1e2d511e3660422da93fce44e6f0a7ca"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":18142,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b835ba31bc4f74