{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d72b678f-d85c-4cc5-87c9-876269c7aeb2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-807fe4d92e56aff9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-m9ioltl1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Model version run lineage in the Model Registry\n\n## Description\n\nRegistered model versions record a link back to the run that produced them,\nso the producing run is identifiable from the Model Registry. This is the\nregistry-side half of enabling a comparison to be opened from the Model\nRegistry.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Store a reference to the producing run on registered model versions, using\n  the registry's existing metadata extension point for structured model\n  version metadata.\n- Expose the run reference on the model version through the registry's REST\n  API so platform surfaces (such as the Dashboard) can read it.\n- The reference must identify the run within its project so it can be\n  resolved back to a specific training or pipeline run.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a registered model version with a known producing run, when the run\n  reference is recorded, then it is retrievable through the model registry\n  REST API.\n- Given the run reference, the producing run is resolvable to a specific run\n  in its project.\n- Given a model version with no run reference, the version remains valid and\n  the absent reference is handled gracefully by API consumers.\n- Recording the run reference is backward compatible with existing model\n  versions and registry clients.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n  them — registry-side storage and exposure of the run reference.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32624,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_t