{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7363954e0856fe2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Model version run lineage in the Model Registry\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Model version run lineage in the Model Registry\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRegistered model versions record a link back to the run that produced them,\n34\tso the producing run is identifiable from the Model Registry. This is the\n35\tregistry-side half of enabling a comparison to be opened from the Model\n36\tRegistry.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Store a reference to the producing run on registered model versions, using\n41\t  the registry's existing metadata extension point for structured model\n42\t  version metadata.\n43\t- Expose the run reference on the model version through the registry's REST\n44\t  API so platform surfaces (such as the Dashboard) can read it.\n45\t- The reference must identify the run within its project so it can be\n46\t  resolved back to a specific training or pipeline run.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given a registered model version with a known producing run, when the run\n51\t  reference is recorded, then it is retrievable through the model registry\n52\t  REST API.\n53\t- Given the run reference, the producing run is resolvable to a specific run\n54\t  in its project.\n55\t- Given a model version with no run reference, the version remains valid and\n56\t  the absent reference is handled gracefully by API consumers.\n57\t- Recording the run reference is backward compatible with existing model\n58\t  versions and registry clients.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n63\t  them — registry-side storage and exposure of the run reference.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6415e67f3853900","agent_id":"ad84a58bf9f85a538","session_id":"44d00f4c-d13b-4638-bc59-4a21076b9c90","uuid":"f16394c3-b477-467d-baba-c60124fbaee5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:50:08.736Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7363954e0856fe2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
