{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f5fd1bf87357804","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E004\n3\ttitle: Pipeline-run comparison data validation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Data Science Pipelines\n6\tteam: RHOAI Pipelines\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Pipeline-run comparison data validation\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tValidation, owned by the Data Science Pipelines team, that pipeline-run\n34\tparameters and metrics are accessible and complete enough for side-by-side\n35\tcomparison and diff as consumed by the Dashboard. Data Science Pipelines is a\n36\tpassive component in this strategy — no code changes are anticipated, because\n37\tpipeline runs and their details are already surfaced through the platform's\n38\texisting pipeline capabilities; this epic validates that assumption for the\n39\tcomparison use case and is owned by a different team than the Dashboard\n40\timplementation.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Enumerate the parameters and metrics exposed for pipeline runs through the\n45\t  existing pipeline run surfaces the Dashboard consumes.\n46\t- Validate retrievability, naming consistency, and completeness of that data\n47\t  for side-by-side comparison and diff of two or more runs.\n48\t- Produce a validation report; any gap is documented with its impact on run\n49\t  comparison and handed to the Dashboard comparison work as