cific run\n54\t  in its project.\n55\t- Given a model version with no run reference, the version remains valid and\n56\t  the absent reference is handled gracefully by API consumers.\n57\t- Recording the run reference is backward compatible with existing model\n58\t  versions and registry clients.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n63\t  them — registry-side storage and exposure of the run reference.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b23f78269ac299fd","agent_id":"a71677e624fcab4c8","session_id":"44d00f4c-d13b-4638-bc59-4a21076b9c90","uuid":"f01c78dc-36b1-44c9-88eb-2fd314c65c4f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:54:32.144Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b60ce8afcd569be0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
